  "title": "Nurdle Pollution Threatens Seabirds Along North East Coast, Charity Warns",
  "summary": "Plastic pollution along the North East coast of England is raising serious concerns for seabirds and marine wildlife after thousands of tiny plastic pellets known as nurdles washed ashore following a shipping accident at the Port of Tyne. The Royal Society for the Protection of Birds (RSPB) has warned that seabirds could face serious health risks if they eat the pellets directly or consume fish that have already ingested them. The incident has highlighted the wider dangers posed by nurdle poll",
